{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rebellious-anecdotal-vaquita","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nExtend the attestation-reuse pattern (already implemented for the completion-verification\nclose gate) to the **code-review** gate, and make reuse **identity-scoped**: an environment\nmust reuse a stored review/completion attestation ONLY when that attestation was minted by the\nSAME signing identity the environment itself signs with. As part of this, evaluate extracting a\n**shared reuse seam** that both the completion gate and the code-review gate call, instead of\ntwo parallel implementations.\n\nDiscovered while implementing standalone completion-verifier recording + close-time reuse\n(`transition_close.record_completion_verdict` + `close_autoresume._reusable_attested_pass`).\n\n## Motivation\n\n- Completion verification already supports: a standalone `verify-completion` run RECORDS a\n  signed `completion-verifier` op-cert on the ticket, and a later same-`--ref` close REUSES it\n  instead of firing a duplicate (billable) verifier run\n  (`close_autoresume._reusable_attested_pass`). Code review (`review-code` / the code-review\n  gate) has no equivalent reuse, so identical reviews are re-run across environments.\n- Reuse across environments with DIFFERENT signing certificates is unsafe. Example: a\n  developer-local `review-code` signs with a local key; the AWS review bot signs with a\n  distinct certificate. The AWS bot must NOT treat the local attestation as its own — reuse\n  must require that the stored attestation's signing identity matches the CONSUMING\n  environment's configured signing identity. Otherwise one environment silently inherits\n  another's trust boundary.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The code-review gate reuses a still-current, same-`ref` code-review attestation instead\n      of re-running the LLM review, mirroring `close_autoresume._reusable_attested_pass`\n      (stricter than validity-on-read: explicit authenticated SHA + material fingerprint that\n      still match the review input; legacy/malformed/stale/unreadable → full review).\n- [ ] Reuse (for BOTH completion and code-review) is IDENTITY-SCOPED: a stored attestation is\n      reused only when its signing identity (the op-cert principal / key fingerprint) equals the\n      consuming environment's configured signing identity. A mismatch (e.g. local cert vs. AWS\n      bot cert) falls through to a fresh signed run under the consuming environment's own\n      identity. This is covered by a test that seeds an attestation under identity A and proves\n      an environment configured with identity B does NOT reuse it.\n- [ ] A DESIGN DECISION is recorded (ADR or ticket comment) on whether to extract a shared\n      reuse seam consumed by both gates. If extracted, both the completion close gate and the\n      code-review gate call it, with no behavior change to the existing completion reuse (its\n      current tests still pass); if NOT extracted, the rejection rationale is documented.\n- [ ] Standalone `review-code` RECORDS its result on the ticket (signs the reusable\n      code-review attestation on an attested pass + emits the sidecar), symmetric with\n      standalone `verify-completion` and `review-plan`, gated by an explicit opt-out\n      (`--no-sign`) and never signing a `local`/uncertifiable verdict.\n- [ ] Portability preserved: reuse and identity-scoping have an operation-linked / in-process\n      basis and are not tied to any single CI provider (`project.portability`).\n\n## Notes / pointers\n\n- Completion reuse consumer: `src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py`\n  (`_reusable_attested_pass`).\n- Completion recording producer: `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`\n  (`record_completion_verdict`, `sign_completion_verdict`).\n- Identity/attestation internals: `src/rebar/attest/opcert.py`, `src/rebar/signing.py`,\n  `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` (`_authoritative_*`, `current_material_fingerprint`).\n- Code-review gate: `src/rebar/llm/code_review/`, MCP/CLI `review-code`.\n- The identity check likely reads the op-cert principal/key-fingerprint from the signed DSSE\n  predicate and compares to the environment's resolved signing binding (see the op-cert service\n  startup binding, `opcert_service/`).","id":"3d86-9fc2-6095-4c69","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["reuse","attestation","code-review","tech-debt"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Identity-scoped attestation reuse for the code-review gate (shared reuse seam)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787535576524805001,"uuid":"313e3b04-004c-4ceb-b9d4-d71a816b684f"}